Programming practices
1. STL algorithm: [ECCopyGen.cpp]
Write a function that copies items from one container to the other container.
2. Implement a container class: ECList and EListNode classes [ECList.cpp,ECListNode.h]
This is a singly linked list. You should support several basic functionalities.
* List traversal
* List insertion/deletion
3. Implement two classes as follows.[ECStudent.h, ECClass.cpp, ECClass.h]
* ECStudent:
Attributes: name and score
Methods: Get and set scores.
* ECClass:
Attributes: list of students
Methods: for grading, etc. Check the provided header files.
4. Practicing constructors: [ECPointerString.cpp]
Now get back to ECStringPtr class. Implement a new function called Duplicate() which return a ECStringPtr which contains a string pointer to a
string which contains two tandem copies of the current string.
One key thing to study is the move constructor.
5. Move constructor again: [ECMatrix.h/cpp]
Implement the constructors (copy and move) for ECMatrix class. The focus is on the differences between copy and move constructors. Investigate
what constructors are called under different situations.